;;;;;; Martini lipid topology for C(d18:1/22:0) SM (BSM), generated using:
; The Martini lipid itp generator version M3.l01  Args are: -alname BSM -alhead 'C P' -allink 'A1 A2' -altail 'tCCC CCCCC'
; WARNING: Autogenerated and not all lipid headgroup and tail combinations have been tested;
;          used with care and see K.B. Pedersen et al. 2024 for guidance.
;
; Description:
;   A general model sphingomyelin (SM) lipid corresponding to atomistic e.g. C(d18:1/22:0) N-behenoyl-D-erythro tails.
; Parameterization:
;   This topology follows the standard Martini 3.0 lipid definitions and building block rules. 
;   Bonded parameters and mapping have been optimized as described in K.B. Pedersen et al. 2024.
; Reference(s): 
; K.B. Pedersen et al., The Martini 3 Lipidome: Expanded and Refined Parameters Improve Lipid Phase Behavior*, 
; ACS Central Science, 2025. doi: 10.1021/acscentsci.5c00755
; P.C.T. Souza et al., Martini 3: A General Purpose Force Field for Coarse-Grained Molecular Dynamics*, 
; Nature Methods, 2021. doi: 10.1038/s41592-021-01098-3
; Created: 2024.07.12
;
; Molecular topology and mapping of indices:
; NC3-PO4-OH1-T1A-C2A-C3A-C4A
;          |
;         AM2-C1B-C2B-C3B-C4B-C5B
;
;  1 - 2 - 3 - 5 - 6 - 7 - 8 
;          |
;          4 - 9 - 10- 11- 12- 13
;
;@INSANE alhead=C P, allink=A1 A2, altail=tCCC CCCCC, alname=BSM, charge=0.0
;@RESNTEST BSM==BSM if: atoms[0]==NC3
;@BEADS NC3 PO4 OH1 AM2 T1A C2A C3A C4A C1B C2B C3B C4B C5B 
;@BONDS NC3-PO4 PO4-OH1 PO4-AM2 OH1-AM2 OH1-T1A T1A-C2A C2A-C3A C3A-C4A AM2-C1B C1B-C2B C2B-C3B C3B-C4B C4B-C5B 
;

